  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arkansas has recorded $697M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Contract activity includes 13,562 awards with an average award size of $51.4K, and obligations fell 44.8% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $403M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $92.9M and the General Services Administration with $46.8M. Construction-related industries lead the state award mix, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction totaling $193M and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction totaling $118M. Large prime awards are concentrated among a few vendors, including BL HARBERT INTERNATIONAL LLC at $102M and ALBERICI CONSTRUCTORS INC at $68.2M. Fiscal-year context shows higher totals in prior years, such as $1.9B in FY24 and $1.5B in FY21, which frames the current year-to-date figure as part of a variable multi-year pattern. These topline figures describe who is buying in Arkansas and which vendors and industries are receiving the largest shares so far in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers in Arkansas right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the biggest buyer, obligating $403M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $92.9M and the General Services Administration obligated $46.8M. The Department of State and the Department of Justice follow with $32.2M and $30.3M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries are getting the most obligations in Arkansas?",
        "body": "BL HARBERT INTERNATIONAL LLC received $102M and ALBERICI CONSTRUCTORS INC received $68.2M in FY2026 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry with $193M, followed by Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction with $118M. Computer Facilities Management Services totaled $32.4M, and All Other Miscellaneous Chemical Product and Preparation Manufacturing totaled $29.7M."
      }
    ]
